**Fix Pocket Notes – Root Cause & Full Patch (Context‑Based Persistence)**  

Below is a **complete, tool‑agnostic recipe** you can follow to make the unfinished draft survive **view switches** and **page reloads**, guarantee **exactly one note per save**, preserve **existing notes**, keep **distinct notes distinct**, and **preserve the UI appearance**.

---

## 1️⃣ Why the draft disappears

| Symptom | Typical cause (no code inspection) |
|---------|------------------------------------|
| Draft gone after navigating to **My notes** | `draft` lives in the **Draft component** state → unmounts on route change. |
| Draft gone after **refresh** | No persistence → state re‑initialized from scratch. |
| “Saving creates **more than one** note” | Save handler attached to both **button click** *and* **Enter key** (or a debounced auto‑save) → duplicate calls. |
| Existing notes lost on reload | Notes stored only in component state, not in `localStorage`. |

**Solution**: Put `notes` and `draft` in a **global context** that survives navigation, and persist both to `localStorage`. The save logic lives in the context, guaranteeing a single‑note creation per user action.

---

## 2️⃣ Implementation Plan

### 2.1 Create a context (`src/context/NotesContext.js`)

*Provides `notes`, `setNotes`, `draft`, `setDraft`, and `saveNote` to the whole app.*

```diff
--- a/src/context/NotesContext.js
+++ b/src/context/NotesContext.js
@@
+import React, { createContext, useState, useEffect, useCallback } from 'react';
+
+/**
+ * NotesContext
+ *   - notes: array of note objects (persistent)
+ *   - draft: current draft text (persistent)
+ *   - saveNote: handler that creates exactly one note and clears draft
+ */
+export const NotesContext = createContext();
+
+export const NotesProvider = ({ children }) => {
+  // ----- State -------------------------------------------------
+  const [notes, setNotes] = useState([]);
+  const [draft, setDraft] = useState('');
+
+  // ----- Load from localStorage on mount -----------------------
+  useEffect(() => {
+    const storedNotes = localStorage.getItem('pocketNotes_notes');
+    if (storedNotes) {
+      setNotes(JSON.parse(storedNotes));
+    }
+    const storedDraft = localStorage.getItem('pocketNotes_draft');
+    if (storedDraft) {
+      setDraft(storedDraft);
+    }
+  }, []);
+
+  // ----- Persist notes -----------------------------------------
+  useEffect(() => {
+    localStorage.setItem('pocketNotes_notes', JSON.stringify(notes));
+  }, [notes]);
+
+  // ----- Persist draft (clear after save) ----------------------
+  useEffect(() => {
+    if (draft === '') {
+      localStorage.removeItem('pocketNotes_draft');
+    } else {
+      localStorage.setItem('pocketNotes_draft', draft);
+    }
+  }, [draft]);
+
+  // ----- Save – one note, clear draft --------------------------
+  const saveNote = useCallback(() => {
+    if (!draft.trim()) return; // ignore empty saves
+
+    const newNote = {
+      id: Date.now().toString(), // simple unique ID
+      content: draft,
+      createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),
+    };
+
+    // Append exactly one note, preserve previous ones
+    setNotes(prev => [...prev, newNote]);
+    setDraft('');
+  }, [draft, setNotes, setDraft]);
+
+  // ----- Provide context --------------------------------------
+  return (
+    <NotesContext.Provider value={{ notes, setNotes, draft, setDraft, saveNote }}>
+      {children}
+    </NotesContext.Provider>
+  );
+};
```

### 2.2 Wrap the app with the provider (`src/App.jsx`)

```diff
--- a/src/App.jsx
+++ b/src/App.jsx
@@
+import React, { useContext } from 'react';
+import { BrowserRouter as Router, Routes, Route, Link } from 'react-router-dom';
+import { NotesProvider, NotesContext } from './context/NotesContext';
+import Draft from './components/Draft';
+import NotesList from './components/NotesList';
+
+// Inner app that consumes the context
+const AppContent = () => {
+  const { draft, setDraft, saveNote } = useContext(NotesContext);
+
+  return (
+    <Router>
+      <nav>
+        <Link to="/draft">Draft</Link> <span> </span>
+        <Link to="/my-notes">My notes</Link>
+      </nav>
+
+      <Routes>
+        <Route
+          path="/draft"
+          element={
+            <Draft
+              draft={draft}
+              setDraft={setDraft}
+              onSave={saveNote}
+            />
+          }
+        />
+        <Route
+          path="/my-notes"
+          element={<NotesList />}
+        />
+      </Routes>
+    </Router>
+  );
+};
+
+const App = () => (
+  <NotesProvider>
+    <AppContent />
+  </NotesProvider>
+);
+
+export default App;
```

